 "test": "The issue's reproduction (kh-rr-8.0.json and its variants). Its truck fix, draft PR #3465 (exact arcs in splitface::with_wall_arcs around prism_local's splits), is unmerged and paused, so there is no merged SolidCraft test yet",
 "summary": "A keyhole cut from the back of a 60 x 30 x 5 plate whose outline is a rounded rectangle (corner radius 4) and whose top edge is filleted R1, which puts torus faces at the corners. The keyhole is an 8 mm entry hole at (30, 10) and a 3.2 mm neck slot to (30, 20), cut 3.3 mm deep from z = 0, then an 8 mm wide head slot over the same centres from z = 1.5, 1.8 deep. The head slot's round end is coaxial with the entry hole and has its radius. On truck the head slot cut fails ('no result'). It works without the fillet, on a plain filleted rectangle, and with an 8.2 mm entry. Steps follow the issue's commands: the entry circle and neck slot (one sketch, all profiles) are one tool, as their union. Volumes are closed form: the fillet's straight runs and torus corners by Pappus, the cuts layer by layer from disc, slot and circular-segment areas (checked against grid integration). Tolerances are 0.1 % of the fillet's removed volume (36.853), well inside the 5.83 between the 8.0 and 8.2 entries.",
